WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:07.070
Until AI takes over everything and we don't need to know anything, it's the best tutor you never had.

00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:09.070
But here's the catch.

00:00:09.740 --> 00:00:12.770
On Tuesday, AI explains something perfectly.

00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:14.630
You feel very smart.

00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:18.010
By Thursday, you're asking the same question again.

00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:21.470
That's because reading answers doesn't create retention.

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:24.690
Teachers have long known that learning needs some friction.

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:26.330
It's like the gym.

00:00:26.260 --> 00:00:28.890
Watch a robot lift weights all day,

00:00:29.490 --> 00:00:30.900
and your arms won't notice.

00:00:31.790 --> 00:00:32.980
And the research agrees.

00:00:33.590 --> 00:00:40.340
In one study, students practising maths with a general chatbot scored 17% lower than students without AI.

00:00:40.850 --> 00:00:45.500
But others used the same model, set up to give hints and hold back answers,

00:00:45.820 --> 00:00:48.370
and they scored as well as those without AI.

00:00:49.100 --> 00:00:53.070
So that's the tutor you'll build: once, for any topic.

00:00:53.840 --> 00:00:57.850
Every lesson starts with one question: what do you want to learn today?
